    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d322">

                <pb facs="0507" n="407" sameAs="frus:frus1934v01/pg407"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500A4B/576: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1934-12-05T12:00:00+09:00">December 5,
                            1934—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received December 4—11:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>269. Reference my telegram No. 267, December 3, 1 p.m., first paragraph, last
                    sentence. My Italian colleague<anchor n="52" xml:id="d322-f1"/> informs me that
                        <pb facs="0508" n="408" xml:id="pg408"/> acting under instructions from Rome
                    he informed the Japanese Government yesterday afternoon very briefly that Italy
                    did not care to join in denunciation of the treaty but that it was ready to
                    participate in any conference to be held under the terms of article 23 after
                    denunciation by Japan.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d322-f1" n="52" xml:id="d322-f1-content">
                <p>Giacinto Auriti.</p>
            </note>
